  "status": "completed",
  "output": "I'll read the file back and validate the geometry using available OGC-compliant tools.Shapely and GDAL aren't installed. Let me try installing shapely for the authoritative OGC `ST_isValid`-style check.The pipe masked the failure. Trying a direct venv install:The system venv is read-only. I'll install shapely into a workspace-local directory instead, run the OGC validity check, then clean up.Shapely 2.2.0 (GEOS-backed, the reference OGC Simple Features engine) is ready. Running the validity check:The GEOS engine confirms invalidity. Let me clean up the temporary libraries so the workspace keeps only your GeoJSON file:## Verdict: INVALID ❌\n\nThe polygon in [invalid_polygon.geojson](/home/agent/workspace/invalid_polygon.geojson) violates the OGC Simple Features specification. I verified this with Shapely 2.2.0 backed by GEOS — the same geometry engine used by PostGIS — rather than judging by eye alone.\n\n**Reason and location**\n\nGEOS reports: `Ring Self-intersection[0 0]` — the exterior ring is self-intersecting at point (0, 0).\n\nTracing the ring coordinates makes the defect precise:\n\n| Index | Point | What happens |\n|-------|-------|--------------|\n| 0 | (0, 0) | Ring start |\n| 1–3 | (2, 0), (2, 2), (0, 2) | Square boundary |\n| 4 | (0, 0) | **Premature closure** — vertex repeated mid-ring |\n| 5 | (1, 1) | Spike apex inside the square |\n| 6 | (0, 0) | Returns to start |\n\nThe OGC spec requires a polygon's exterior ring to be **closed** *and* **simple** (no self-intersection other than the mandatory first-point-equals-last-point closure). This ring is closed but not simple:\n\n1. **Repeated vertex at (0, 0)** — index 4 closes the ring, but vertices continue after it, so (0, 0) is visited three times (indices 0, 4, 6) where multiple segments meet and cross.\n2. **Zero-area spike** — the legs (0, 0)→(1, 1)→(0, 0) traverse the same segment in both directions, an out-and-back excursion that adds no area and creates overlapping edges.\n\nProgrammatic results: `geom.is_valid == False`, `geom.exterior.is_ring == False` (closed yet non-simple). Most GIS software will either refuse to load it or silently repair it — for example by buffering by 0 or dropping the spike, which would yield the plain 2×2 square.",
  "error": null,
